# Fractions Skill Score (FSS) Example

This example demonstrates how to aggregate NBRCNT (neighborhood continuous statistics)
data from MET stat files and compute the Fractions Skill Score (FSS) using VCasT. It uses
`NAMnest_mem000` composite reflectivity (REFC) at four thresholds (>=20, >=30, >=40,
>=50 dBZ) and five neighborhood sizes (`interp_pnts`: 9, 25, 81, 361, 729), grouped by
model/fcst_var/fcst_lead/fcst_thresh/interp_pnts.

## Data Aggregation:
This step processes the MET NBRCNT stat files and aggregates FSS into an output file.

## Plot Generation (optional, manual):
`plot.yaml` plots FSS vs. lead time for the >=20 dBZ threshold, one line per neighborhood
size. It expects one input file per neighborhood size (`agg_20_9.data`, `agg_20_25.data`,
...), which `create_files.sh` produces by splitting `agg.data` on threshold and
`interp_pnts`. This split step is not part of the automated test suite (only the
aggregation step is), so it needs to be run manually before plotting.

## Commands

1. Aggregate Data
Run the following command to process the MET stat files. This produces
`filtered_output.data` (reformatted rows), `vars.data`, and `agg.data`.

```bash
# Aggregates MET NBRCNT stat files and creates the aggregated data file
vcast NBRCNT.yaml
```

2. Split the Aggregated Data by Threshold/Neighborhood Size
Run the helper script to split `agg.data` into the per-threshold, per-`interp_pnts` files
that `plot.yaml` reads from:

```bash
# Creates agg_<threshold>_<interp_pnts>.data files from agg.data
./create_files.sh
```

3. Generate the FSS Plot
Once the split files exist, run the following command to generate the plot:

```bash
# Generates the FSS plot using the split aggregated data
vcast plot.yaml
```
